diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index 795940a..2c62f58 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -41,3 +41,13 @@ Bots are `User` records with `role: :bot` (`User::Role`), implemented via the `U
 - Enforcement:
   - `app/views/bots/index.html.erb` hides `"Add a chat bot"` and displays `"You’ve reached the limit of ..."` when `Current.user.bot_limit_reached?`.
   - `BotsController` enforces `before_action :ensure_can_create_bot, only: %i[ new create ]`, refusing `GET /bots/new` and `POST /bots` with `403 Forbidden` (rendering `bots/index`).
+
+## Automatic Suspension & Rate Limiting
+- Fixed limits in `User::Bot` (no account settings):
+  - Flooding: max `10` messages (`FLOOD_MESSAGE_LIMIT`) in any `10` seconds (`FLOOD_WINDOW`), shared across API posts (`Bots::MessagesController`) and synchronous webhook replies (`Bot::Webhook#handle_response`).
+  - Over-limit message is rejected and starts a `30`-second cooldown (`COOLDOWN_DURATION`), during which the posting endpoint returns `429 Too Many Requests` with `Retry-After` (remaining seconds) and webhook replies are not posted.
+  - `5` more attempts to post during the same cooldown (`COOLDOWN_SUSPEND_ATTEMPTS`) suspend the bot; a new cooldown resets the attempt count.
+  - Failing webhooks: any non-`2xx` response, timeout, or connection error increments `consecutive_webhook_failures`. `10` consecutive failures (`WEBHOOK_FAILURE_SUSPEND_THRESHOLD`) suspend the bot; any `2xx` response resets the counter to `0`.
+- All rate-limit and failure counters are persisted in the database (`users` columns) and updated under `with_lock` so tests (`cache_store = :null_store`) and concurrent requests behave deterministically.
+- Suspension preserves `status: :active` and uses `suspended_at` + `suspension_reason` so suspended bots keep their rooms and messages, still count toward `bots_per_member`, remain visible on `/bots` with `"Suspended"` and the reason, return `403 Forbidden` from the posting endpoint, and receive no webhooks (`User.with_webhook` excludes suspended bots and `Bot::Webhook#deliverable?` re-checks `!bot.suspended?`).
+- Reactivation: `Bots::ReactivationsController#create` (`POST /bots/:bot_id/reactivation`), restricted to administrators via `ensure_can_administer`, clears suspension, cooldown, failure counts, and recent post timestamps. On `/bots`, only administrators see the `"Reactivate"` button (with `turbo_confirm`).
diff --git a/test/controllers/bots/messages_controller_test.rb b/test/controllers/bots/messages_controller_test.rb
